# 高频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List03核心词汇

{{maintain}}{/meɪnˈteɪn/}{维持；维护}{It is important to maintain a healthy lifestyle.}
{{manipulate}}{/məˈnɪpjuleɪt/}{操纵；操作}{The data was manipulated to support a false conclusion.}}
{{measure}}{/ˈmeʒər/}{测量；措施}{We need to take measures to reduce pollution.}}
{{mechanism}}{/ˈmekənɪzəm/}{机制；机械装置}{The brain has its own defense mechanism against stress.}}
{{media}}{/ˈmiːdiə/}{媒体；媒介}{Social media has changed the way we communicate.}}
{{medical}}{/ˈmedɪkl/}{医学的；医疗的}{Medical research has saved millions of lives.}}
{{mental}}{/ˈmentl/}{精神的；心理的}{Mental health is as important as physical health.}}
{{method}}{/ˈmeθəd/}{方法；办法}{We need a more effective method of teaching.}}
{{military}}{/ˈmɪlɪtəri/}{军事的；军队}{The country increased its military spending.}}
{{modify}}{/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ/}{修改；改变}{We need to modify our approach based on new data.}}
{{monitor}}{/ˈmɒnɪtər/}{监控；监视}{Doctors monitor patients' vital signs continuously.}}
{{moral}}{/ˈmɒrəl/}{道德的；道义的}{There are moral implications to consider in this debate.}}
{{motivate}}{/ˈməʊtɪveɪt/}{激励；激发}{Good leaders motivate their teams to achieve goals.}}
{{mutual}}{/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/}{相互的；共同的}{Mutual respect is the basis of any good relationship.}}
{{negative}}{/ˈneɡətɪv/}{消极的；否定的}{Don't let negative thoughts hold you back.}}
{{negotiate}}{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt/}{谈判；协商}{The unions are negotiating with management for better pay.}}
{{network}}{/ˈnetwɜːk/}{网络；网状系统}{Building a professional network is essential for career growth.}}
{{neutral}}{/ˈnjuːtrəl/}{中立的；中性的}{Switzerland has remained neutral in many conflicts.}}
{{nevertheless}}{/ˌnevəðəˈles/}{然而；不过}{The task was difficult; nevertheless, we completed it on time.}}
{{norm}}{/nɔːm/}{规范；准则}{Social norms vary from culture to culture.}}
{{notion}}{/ˈnəʊʃn/}{概念；想法}{The notion that money equals happiness is a misconception.}}
{{nuclear}}{/ˈnjuːkliər/}{核的；原子核的}{Nuclear energy is a controversial topic.}}
{{obtain}}{/əbˈteɪn/}{获得；得到}{She obtained her degree from a prestigious university.}}
{{obvious}}{/ˈɒbviəs/}{明显的；显而易见的}{The answer was obvious to everyone in the room.}}
{{occupy}}{/ˈɒkjupaɪ/}{占据；占领}{Reading occupies most of my free time.}}
{{occur}}{/əˈkɜːr/}{发生；出现}{Accidents can occur when people are not careful.}}
{{operate}}{/ˈɒpəreɪt/}{操作；经营}{The company operates in over 30 countries.}}
{{opponent}}{/əˈpəʊnənt/}{对手；反对者}{She defeated her opponent in the final match.}}
{{opportunity}}{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti/}{机会；时机}{This is a great opportunity for career development.}}
{{oppose}}{/əˈpəʊz/}{反对；对抗}{Many citizens opposed the new tax policy.}
